        "original_id": "30664cd5-5fd7-5ccd-aabc-b040aead332e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Texas Raiders, Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress, B-17G-95-DL\n- Places: General Aviation Services, Conroe North Houston Regional Airport, Conroe, Texas, Australia, Melbourne, Philippines\n- People: Douglas MacArthur\n- Organizations: United States Army Air Corps\n- Events: Douglas MacArthur's escape from the Philippines\n\nFacts:\n- The Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress was developed in the 1930s for the United States Army Air Corps as a four-engine heavy bomber.\n- The Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress was introduced in 1938 and later evolved through numerous design advances.\n- The Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress became the third-most produced bomber of all time, behind the B-24 and the multirole Ju 88.\n- During Douglas MacArthur's escape from the Philippines, Douglas MacArthur and his party flew to Australia in a pair of Boeing B-17 Flying Fortresses and arrived in Melbourne by train on 21 March.\n- Texas Raiders is an American Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress and a Douglas-Long Beach built B-17G-95-DL.\n- Texas Raiders is hangared at General Aviation Services at Conroe North Houston Regional Airport in Conroe, Texas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
